# Store and check out every text file as LF, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF docker-entrypoint.sh
# makes the shebang "#!/bin/sh\r", so the kernel looks for an interpreter named
# "/bin/sh\r" and the container dies at startup. The committed blobs are LF, so
# this only ever reproduces on a local Windows build, never in CI.
#
# Applied to everything rather than a list of extensions: nothing here is built
# by Windows-native tooling, so a file type added later is covered by default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The files the rule exists for: a stray CR breaks these at runtime, not build.
*.sh                    text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh    text eol=lf
*.spec                  text eol=lf
Dockerfile              text eol=lf
Makefile                text eol=lf
.github/**              text eol=lf

# Pinned rather than sniffed: a misdetection corrupts these on checkout.
*.png                   binary
*.jpg                   binary
*.jpeg                  binary
*.ico                   binary
